                    <history>
                        <origin>
                            <origDate calendar="Gregorian" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1199">s.
                                xii</origDate>
                        </origin>
                        <provenance type="rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1001">Cropthorne,
                                Worcestershire. Parish church</orgName>
                            <p>The index card records the following provenance evidence: <q>Iste
                                    liber est magistri <persName role="fmo">Michael</persName>
                                    rectoris ecclesie de Cropthorne &amp; traditur <persName
                                        role="fmo">Ade de Furches</persName> diacono usque ad Festum
                                    sancti Johannis Baptiste anno Domini mº ccº lxxº nono</q>.
                                However, this is insufficient grounds for an attribution to the
                                parish church. Compare the preface to MLGB2, p. viii: 'Books
                                belonging to the secular clergy [...] are not included'. A later
                                pencil note on the index card notes: <q>not within scope</q>.</p>
                            This manuscript is not listed as a rejected parish church book in either
                            MLGB2 or the Supplement. This might be because the index card was not
                            filed in the parish church section, but instead in the main sequence
                            under the letter 'C' (where it was found during data reconciliation work
                            in 2026).</provenance>
                    </history>
